{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQUzptTGUikAhRtBNZRS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Assess: still grill · Strict. Questions 2–5 are still open, and your answer raises two small new points.\n\nLocked in: **the customer picks 2, 3, or 4 equal installments.**\n\nTwo follow-ups on that:\n\n**1a. Spacing and when they can choose.** *Recommend:* installments are a month apart, and the first one is due on the invoice's current `dueDate`. The customer can choose a plan only while the invoice is `sent` and unpaid. Once a plan is chosen it's fixed (no switching from 3 to 4).\n\n**1b. \"Equal\" when the total doesn't split evenly.** For example, $100.00 ÷ 3 = 3333.33… cents. *Recommend:* every installment is the same rounded-down amount, and the last one takes the leftover cents (3333 / 3333 / 3334), so they add up exactly to the total.\n\nStill need your call on these (short versions; full reasoning is above):\n\n2. **Interest or plan fee.** Recommend **none**. Charging one can bring in consumer-credit rules.\n3. **Late fee on a missed installment.** Recommend **2% of that installment**, once per missed installment, instead of 2% of the whole invoice.\n4. **Payments and status.** Recommend:\n   - payments go to the earliest unpaid installment first, and any extra rolls forward\n   - `overdue` while any installment is past due, back to `sent` once caught up\n   - paying everything off early is allowed\n5. **Reminders.** Recommend one reminder **3 days before each unpaid installment**.\n\nA quick \"yes to all recommendations\" works, or tell me just the ones you'd change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1346,"cache_read_input_tokens":34628,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1346},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"s